# Development-only material. The npm package is built from runtime paths;
# fixtures, benchmarks, docs, receipts, and generated output stay local.
#
# test/ is deliberately NOT ignored (2026-07-28). npm publication is already
# bounded twice over — package.json "files" allowlists only bin/ engine/
# install.* CHANGELOG README, and the release CI re-scans the packed tarball —
# so ignoring test/ never protected the published package. What it did do was
# hide 23 of 52 suites from GitHub, where smoke.sh's `if [ -f ]` loop then
# skipped them silently: the release gate reported "66 passed" locally while
# roughly 41 ran in CI. A test that cannot run in CI is not a gate.
tests/
**/tests/
benchmarks/
**/benchmarks/
